From 24e56bcc6637950a14e55ef3a6b804a7894980b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 04:18:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 412/417] Gui: a command run before its action is made gets its
 action first

Running a group command from Python or the command search while its
toolbar is not shown (the unified window shows its own bar) crashed:
PartDesign_CompPrimitiveAdditive read its action group, which was not
made yet (SIGSEGV in ActionGroup::actions; found by a sweep running
every command). Command::_invoke makes the action first; some 59 group
commands read their action the same way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Gui/Command.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Gui/Command.cpp b/src/Gui/Command.cpp
index aec29a167..2c02071ab 100644
--- a/src/Gui/Command.cpp
+++ b/src/Gui/Command.cpp
@@ -477,6 +477,10 @@ void Command::invoke(int i, TriggerSource trigger)
 
 void Command::_invoke(int id, bool disablelog)
 {
+    // a command run before its action was made (from Python or the command search, its
+    // toolbar not shown yet): group commands read their action and crashed (a GUI sweep of
+    // every command: PartDesign_CompPrimitiveAdditive)
+    initAction();
     try {
         // set the application module type for the macro
         getGuiApplication()->macroManager()->setModule(sAppModule);
-- 
